<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005L0015X_08_0008" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIT00000">
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Evaporator Temperature Sensor (Fin))</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), follow the prompts on the screen to display the "ECU Data Monitor" screen and check the computer data.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[Diagnosis menu screen: Body → A/C → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.56in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.02in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Item Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference Value</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Evaporator Temperature Sensor (Fin)</ptxt>
<ptxt>[FIN]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Displayed in range -29.7 to 59.55°C</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When open: (-29.7°C) displayed</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When shorted: (59.55°C) displayed</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Result</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="right">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Does not display same value as evaporator temperature sensor surrounding temperature</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Displays same value as evaporator temperature sensor surrounding temperature</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005L0015X_08_0009" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000005L0015X_08_0011" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005L0015X_08_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIU00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Cooler Thermistor NO.1 (Evaporator Temperature Sensor)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the cooler thermistorNO.1(evaporator temperature sensor) connector from the air conditioner harness assembly.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals of the cooler thermistorNO.1(evaporator temperature sensor).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E146761J01" width="2.775699831in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Ambient Temperature]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="8" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-10°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>7.30 to 9.10 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-5°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5.65 to 6.95 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>0°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4.40 to 5.35 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>5°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>3.40 to 4.15 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.70 to 3.25 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>15°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>2.14 to 2.58 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.71 to 2.05 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>25°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.38 to 1.64 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>30°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1.11 to 1.32 kΩ</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Touching the temperature sensor part will affect it with body heat and prevent a correct judgment, so hold the connector side when inspecting the sensor.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Allow the sensor to adjust to the ambient temperature before inspecting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005L0015X_08_0010" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005L0015X_08_0012" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005L0015X_08_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIV00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Air Conditioner Harness Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
